+- **The measure is the un-forwardable pile**, not total resident traffic. In
+  this sim a packet at a node forwards unconditionally when a route exists
+  (the per-hop forward pass never throttles a node) — so a node's honest load
+  is the backlog that FAILED to forward (waiting_ticks ≥ 1). Flow congestion
+  surfaces on pipes (E9 lane sheds + the 4.1 pipe pressure), never as a node
+  pile. The alternative — a transit-inclusive "utilization" (all at-node
+  packets) — was implemented, measured, and **rejected**: the health_win
+  prepared fan's routers hold 0–3 one-tick transit packets (75–225% of
+  router_basic throughput) even mid-surge with the meter at 100. Any
+  transit-inclusive measure makes the healthy map scream, violating the
+  "keep it quiet at 🟢" canon. The un-forwardable pile is 0 on healthy
+  traffic by construction and climbs with every real drowning (an unconnected
+  growth-born terminal, a severed route) — the early-warning signal.
+- **The thresholds are the 4.1 strain thresholds (70/90, data-driven in
+  balance.json `warnings`) BY CHOICE.** The card requires the health surface
+  to be "coherent with (not contradicting) the forecast's idea of strain" —
+  sharing the `warnings` block makes the coherence by construction (the
+  arrays are provably equal on every live slot, pinned by a test). It also
+  keeps `catalog_hash` untouched: a dedicated `node_health` block would
+  re-bless every golden (catalog edits are golden-poisoned — every byte folds
+  into the hash). No balance.json change lands in this PR.
+- **Deterministic**: same inputs → same states. No wall-clock, no RNG (the
+  measure reads only flow.packets + topology + catalogs at the step boundary).
+
+## Derive-don't-record proof
+
+The health states never enter the replay log or the save format — no
+LOG_VERSION bump, no new serialized bytes:
+
+1. **The state is a pure function of per-tick measurements** (flow.packets +
+   topology + catalogs). The serializer writes only
+   `node_strain/pipe_strain/forecast/active` from `Crisis_State` — the new
+   `node_health` array is structurally excluded (verified in
+   `core/serialize.odin`).
+2. **Replay identity**: a replayed run (same seed + action log) derives the
+   byte-identical health timeline — pinned by
+   `test_node_health_replay_derives_identically` (live == replay levels at
+   every tick AND the hash sequence).
+3. **Negative control**: the state dump is byte-identical before/after
+   mutating `node_health` — if a future serializer ever writes it, the pin
+   goes red.
+4. **Why a separate array and not the existing `node_strain`**: the 4.1
+   strain IS serialized (its warning events ride the T1). The card explicitly
+   forbids the health state from entering the save format, so the surface has
+   its own never-recorded home. The separation is also the future-proofing:
+   the health thresholds can be re-tuned independently without re-blessing
+   the warning goldens. Today the measurement is shared for coherence; the
+   SEPARATION is the contract.
+
