-## Decisions & rationale
-
-- **CSV over JSONL** — byte-determinism + diffability are the contract; integer-only
-  rows make CSV trivially identical and plain-tool diffable. JSONL's structure
-  doesn't pay for its formatting-drift risk (the project's JSON-for-state trap class
-  is already deleted).
-- **Per-sim-tick emission** — a paused wall tick is stable state, and the drop sites
-  are per-step scratch; recording a paused "record" would fabricate drops. Live and
-  replay step the same sim ticks (pause = run setup), so replay-identity holds.
-- **Load columns are the bundle, lane columns are the pipe** — the pooled link
-  (2.1) is the honest capacity unit the flow serves; a member pipe's "load" IS its
-  bundle's. D rows replicate a shed bundle's drops to every live member (the pool
-  shed them).
-- **Overlay data = stream data** — both read the same `stats_compute` record; the
-  numbers under `D` are the numbers the harness byte-compares.
-- **App stream is written at exit** — a killed process loses the session's stream
-  (the harness path is the deterministic artifact; the app's is the same derivation,
-  same format, for the same seed+commands).
-- **App restart appends** — a restart mints a fresh seed and appends the new run's
-  ticks to the same stream file (tick restarts at 1; the sim_hash column — the per-
-  tick T1 hash, which folds the seed — disambiguates runs; no seed column is
-  written, by design the G row carries tick/gen/hash/score/meter). The overlay is
-  per-run (the record is destroyed on restart).
-- **The overlay is a debug surface, not a golden** — compile-excluded from harness
-  builds by construction; `overlay-check` PNGs land in gitignored `bin/`.
-- **Meter column** — rides raw (health.odin pins the disabled state at 100; 0 would
